  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "Evidence: The multimodal concat model (config_016, acc=0.527) only marginally outperforms RNA-only (config_001, acc=0.485), while image-only (config_010, acc=0.208) is very weak. This raises a critical uncertainty: is the modest multimodal gain due to a weak image encoder (ResNet50) failing to extract useful signal, or is the image modality fundamentally limited? Question tested: config_022 swaps only the image encoder from ResNet50 to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L while keeping everything else identical to config_016 (pca_n2000, concat, singleprofile). This clean A/B comparison isolates the image encoder's contribution. Why best next experiment: Resolving whether a stronger image encoder unlocks meaningful multimodal gains is the highest-priority design question. A large improvement would validate further investment in multimodal + ViT-L configurations; a flat result would redirect the budget toward RNA-side improvements (multiprofile, alternative encoders). No other single experiment reduces this key uncertainty as efficiently."
}

